{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03OK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$E$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathbf{Z}[E]$", "MATH_0003": "$E$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathbf{Z}[E] = \\bigoplus_{e \\in E} \\mathbf{Z}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathbf{Z}[E]$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathbf{Z}$", "MATH_0007": "$E$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2c417470b0a492f19476c14baf640d2593daf518304008a80596ffe269cc3549", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e649c766df4728db77db38fdf39890fb89b29ea5b3cb3003ffffb85694f63bd4", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nGiven a set <MATH_0001> we denote (in this section)\n<MATH_0002> the free abelian group on <MATH_0003>. In a formula\n<MATH_0004>, i.e., <MATH_0005> is\na free <MATH_0006>-module having a basis consisting of the elements of <MATH_0007>.\nUsing this notation we introduce the free abelian presheaf on a\npresheaf of sets.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bc7123fbdf0ad064cd57d78d2d7131dfddc8388888d0025c157a3c57d25160e7", "unit_id": "tag:03OK:prose-0005"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03OK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathbf{Z}_\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\mathbf{Z}_\\mathcal{G}(U)\n=\n\\mathbf{Z}[\\mathcal{G}(U)]\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{G} = h_U$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathbf{Z}_U = \\mathbf{Z}_{h_U}$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-free-abelian-presheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ed2accca9c55663706c55c22ccb8e1ce8ca0c9aefbc273a33eda96883b8bfeaa", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:13c3c03651afba54d8779584084c14f31d19590002bf85577fe4d933603414dc", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category.\nGiven a presheaf of sets <MATH_0002>, we define the\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>free abelian presheaf on <MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>,\ndenoted <MATH_0004>, by the rule\n<MATH_0005>\nfor <MATH_0006>\nwith restriction maps induced by the restriction maps of <MATH_0007>.\nIn the special case <MATH_0008> we write simply\n<MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:816a5b2332e129850c610fefdcaa6f33083a67bfbffc87c26819892bcf936205", "unit_id": "tag:03OO:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03OK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{G} \\mapsto \\mathbf{Z}_\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\textit{PAb}(\\mathcal{C}) \\to \\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\Hom_{\\textit{PAb}(\\mathcal{C})}(\\mathbf{Z}_U, \\mathcal{F})\n=\n\\Hom_{\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})}(h_U, \\mathcal{F})\n=\n\\mathcal{F}(U)\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9a7e4e4062f3ddd93b033512cd12f5cf61c8daa23af5e73fd93b17ea34deb369", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0e8b15b80923448252d2b043dff7aeb25c14e346ea680c796d6a096ca30848e4", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe functor <MATH_0001> is left adjoint to the\nforgetful functor <MATH_0002>.\nThus, for any presheaf <MATH_0003>, there is a canonical isomorphism\n<MATH_0004>\nthe last equality by the Yoneda lemma. In particular, we have the following\nresult.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3f2113a6a6c47849b4314d988c599b1f024b73bb14839eeb4673bd2f675a0f9e", "unit_id": "tag:03OK:prose-0006"}
